WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
Step inside many Catholic churches.

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:07.040
Just by the door stands a
stone basin of water: the font.

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.350
Now look ahead.

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.580
Far away, raised up so
everyone can see it,

5
00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.100
stands the altar.

6
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:18.140
And seen from above, many churches
are built in one shape: a cross.

7
00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:22.520
So why is the font by the door,
and the altar at the far end?

8
00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:26.720
In this mission, you'll meet the
altar, the lectern and the tabernacle,

9
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.040
and what each says about redemption.

10
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:33.860
Then you'll weigh up a bold claim: that
Catholics do not need a special building

11
00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.400
to worship God.

12
00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.110
Your mission: find out why a Catholic
church places the font by the door and the

13
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.640
altar at the far end.
